\vspace{0.05in}
Dear Hiring Team,

Denmark's Joint Government Digital Strategy commits 80 million DKK through 2029 to digital
sovereignty: reducing vendor dependence and keeping authorities in control of their own solutions
and data. I made a much smaller version of that call this year. Asked to automate invoice
processing at SUSS, I ran a Llama 3 3B model on local hardware rather than a cloud API, because the
documents were too sensitive to leave the network. I am applying for the Student Assistant position
in AI/LLM Solutions, available 15 to 20 hours weekly from August.

That choice cost some output quality and a little speed, and was still right: staff went from a
ten-minute manual workflow to a one-click review across more than fifty documents, and the data
never left the university. The workflow itself is gated -- a human approves each extraction and a
digital signature is applied before anything sends. I also built the measurement side, an evaluation
harness scoring model output against rubrics, so the department could say whether a tool was
reliable enough to trust, not merely that it ran.

At Yap Motor I was the first machine-learning hire and inherited no AI infrastructure. I built the
company's first system, a retrieval pipeline over their repair manuals that 24 mechanics query
daily; it remains in use six months on, at 90 percent retrieval precision measured against a month
of mechanic feedback rather than a benchmark.

What draws me to this role is the enablement half. I designed and taught a machine-learning
workshop for 207 participants, writing every slide, annotated notebook and graded exercise myself,
and have presented AI evaluations and cost-benefit analyses to non-technical senior leadership. I
noticed the Embassy helped organise Neural Networking: Nordic-Singapore AI in March, and would
gladly help prepare that kind of session internally. As a Singapore citizen I need no work pass, and
am ready to complete the Certificate of Clearance and Danish security clearance. I would welcome a
conversation about the setup you have in mind.

\vspace{0.15in}

Sincerely, \\[6pt]
Victor Chua \\
Nanyang Technological University

