Dear Members of the Selection Committee,

I am writing to express my enthusiastic interest in the \textbf{World Model Research Intern} position at Tencent's Level Infinite AI Lab in Singapore. As a Computer Science undergraduate at Nanyang Technological University in the Turing AI Scholars Programme (TAISP), my research focuses on multimodal generative models, deep learning vision pipelines, and interactive agent architectures. Level Infinite's pioneer work in video generation and virtual world synthesis directly aligns with my passion for advancing multimodal Generative AI.

In my independent project, Drum Hub, I developed a complete deep learning computer vision pipeline from raw data acquisition to model deployment. I curated a custom labelled vision dataset from scratch using synthetic data generation and image augmentations, then trained a dual-head MobileNetV3 Optical Music Recognition model via two-phase transfer learning. I evaluated the model performance and published the trained weights on HuggingFace. Additionally, I architected an Agentic AI system using LangGraph with state machines and structured tool schemas, establishing a solid foundation in interactive agent design.

My industry experience further demonstrates my capability in multimodal AI and generative model workflows. At SUSS Digital Solutions \& AI, I automated document and video content categorization by integrating TwelveLabs multimodal video analysis pipelines and engineered an on-premises LLM inference pipeline for privacy-sensitive data. Furthermore, during my machine learning internship at Yap Motor, I architected and deployed a production RAG system serving 24 mechanics daily. These experiences have equipped me with strong PyTorch engineering, data preprocessing, and model optimization capabilities.

I am eager to contribute my multimodal vision, dataset engineering, and PyTorch skills to Tencent's World Model research team for the 2027 summer internship period (May 11 -- August 11, 2027). Thank you for your time and consideration.

\vspace{1.5em}

